---
name: clawsight
description: Run the WSInsight engine family (wsinsight, sptxinsight, hplot, kurtorank, wsitrain) in Docker and drive them through MCP proxy tools
---

# ClawSight Skill (Hermes)

ClawSight starts Docker containers for five analysis engines and proxies tool
calls to the MCP server running inside each one. You never install an engine;
you start its container and call its tools.

| Engine | What it does | GPU | Default port |
| ------ | ------------ | --- | ------------ |
| `wsinsight` | Whole-slide pathology: tissue segmentation, patching, GPU cell inference, neighborhood composition, niche discovery, GeoJSON/OME-CSV export | yes | 8765 |
| `sptxinsight` | Spatial transcriptomics: AnnData ingest, cell typing, niche discovery, H-Plot, ligand-receptor (CCI) | yes | 8766 |
| `hplot` | Signed-distance boundary profiling: cluster-mass permutation tests, GAM effect sizes | no | 8767 |
| `kurtorank` | Unsupervised subtype annotation and marker ranking for gene-limited panels | no | 8768 |
| `wsitrain` | Headless end-to-end training of WSInsight CellViT heads | yes | 8769 |

---

## 1. The five tools, per engine

Every engine exposes exactly the same five tools. Nothing engine-specific is
hard-coded — a new backend is one registry row.

| Tool | Purpose | Blocks? |
| ---- | ------- | ------- |
| `<engine>_start` | Start the container + MCP server, then list its tools | sync |
| `<engine>_stop` | Stop and remove the container | sync |
| `<engine>_status` | Is it running? which URL? how many tools? | sync |
| `<engine>_list_tools` | Live tool catalog; pass `tool=` for one tool's full schema | sync |
| `<engine>_call` | Invoke any tool the container exposes | sync wrapper; the underlying tool may be a job |

So the full surface is 25 tools: `wsinsight_start`, `wsinsight_stop`,
`wsinsight_status`, `wsinsight_list_tools`, `wsinsight_call`, and the same five
for `sptxinsight`, `hplot`, `kurtorank`, `wsitrain`.

**Tool catalogs are discovered live, never hard-coded.** Whatever the installed
image supports is what you can call. This is why `<engine>_list_tools` is the
authority on parameter names — not this document, and not your memory of the
engine's CLI.

### 1.1 `<engine>_start`

| Parameter | Type | Required | Default | Description |
| --------- | ---- | -------- | ------- | ----------- |
| `data_dir` | string | **yes** | — | Host directory mounted at `/workspace` inside the container. Must exist. |
| `gpu_ids` | string | no | all GPUs | Comma-separated GPU ids, e.g. `"0,1"`. Rejected by CPU-only engines. |
| `port` | integer | no | engine default | Host and container port for the MCP server. |
| `container_name` | string | no | `clawsight-<engine>` | Container name. |
| `max_concurrent` | integer | no | server default | Maximum concurrent jobs the server will run. |
| `experimental` | boolean | no | engine default | Expose experimental sub-commands as tools. |

On success it prints the container id, image, `mcp_url`, the `data_dir` →
`/workspace` mapping, and the discovered tool list.

It **replaces** any container of the same name (stop + rm first), so calling it
twice is safe.

Your uid/gid are passed in as `HOST_UID` / `HOST_GID`, so outputs are written
as you rather than as root.

### 1.2 `<engine>_stop`

| Parameter | Type | Required | Default | Description |
| --------- | ---- | -------- | ------- | ----------- |
| `container_name` | string | no | `clawsight-<engine>` | Container to stop and remove. |

### 1.3 `<engine>_status`

No parameters. Reports whether the container is running, the MCP URL, and how
many tools were discovered. When it is not running it tells you the exact
`<engine>_start` call to make.

### 1.4 `<engine>_list_tools`

| Parameter | Type | Required | Default | Description |
| --------- | ---- | -------- | ------- | ----------- |
| `tool` | string | no | — | Return the full JSON input schema for this one tool instead of the summary list. |

Call it with no arguments for the catalog; call it with `tool=` before using a
tool whose parameters you are unsure of.

### 1.5 `<engine>_call`

| Parameter | Type | Required | Default | Description |
| --------- | ---- | -------- | ------- | ----------- |
| `tool` | string | **yes** | — | Tool name exactly as reported by `<engine>_list_tools`. |
| `arguments` | object | no | `{}` | Arguments object for that tool, matching its input schema. |

Argument names are the engine's CLI parameter names in **snake_case**
(`wsi_dir`, `results_dir`, `batch_size`, `export_geojson`). The engines' MCP
adapters translate them to kebab-case flags. **No positional arguments are
supported anywhere in the family.**

---

## 2. Standard Workflow

Always start the container first — nothing else works until it is running.

```
1. wsinsight_start({"data_dir": "/data/slides"})
      -> mounts /data/slides at /workspace and prints the tool list

2. wsinsight_list_tools({"tool": "run"})
      -> the exact input schema, so you do not guess parameter names

3. wsinsight_call({"tool": "run", "arguments": {
       "wsi_dir": "/workspace/images",
       "results_dir": "/workspace/out",
       "model": "CellViT-SAM-H-x40"}})
      -> {"job_id": "..."} for long-running tools

4. wsinsight_call({"tool": "job_status", "arguments": {"job_id": "..."}})
      -> poll until a terminal state

5. wsinsight_call({"tool": "job_logs", "arguments": {"job_id": "..."}})
      -> on failure, read this BEFORE retrying

6. wsinsight_stop({})
```

---

## 3. Paths Are Container Paths

`data_dir` is a **host** directory; everything inside the container sees it as
`/workspace`.

After `wsinsight_start({"data_dir": "/data/slides"})`, the host file
`/data/slides/images/a.svs` is `/workspace/images/a.svs` in every subsequent
`_call`. **Passing host paths to `_call` will fail.**

The rule applies to every path argument — inputs, outputs, model directories,
manifests.

---

## 4. Long-Running vs Immediate

Pipeline tools (`run`, `patch`, `infer`, `ncomp`, `niche`, `screen`, training
stages, …) return a `job_id` immediately. Short tools (`export`, `reg`,
`niche_profile`, `plot`, …) block and return their result directly.

Which is which is engine-specific and is stated in each tool's description in
`<engine>_list_tools`. Do not assume.

Job management goes through `_call` like any other tool:

| Tool name | Purpose |
| --------- | ------- |
| `job_status` | Current state of one job. Poll this until terminal. |
| `job_logs` | Stream output. Accepts `since_line` / `max_lines`. |
| `cancel_job` | Stop a running job. |
| `list_jobs` | Every job the server knows about. |

Discipline that avoids the common failure modes:

- Poll `job_status` until it reports a terminal state (succeeded / failed /
  cancelled). Do not assume completion from elapsed time.
- On failure, fetch `job_logs` **before** retrying.
- Never re-issue the same job while a prior one is still running.

---

## 5. GPUs and Concurrency

`wsinsight`, `sptxinsight` and `wsitrain` accept `gpu_ids` on `_start`
(`"0,1"`; omit for all GPUs). `hplot` and `kurtorank` are CPU-only and reject
the option.

Set `max_concurrent` to the number of GPUs you gave the container. Leaving it
unbounded on a single GPU makes concurrent jobs contend and can OOM.

---

## 6. Experimental Tools

`wsinsight` and `sptxinsight` hide some sub-commands unless the container was
started with `experimental: true` (the default for both — the flag sets the
engine's `*_EXPERIMENTAL` env var and adds `--experimental` to the server
command). `hplot`, `kurtorank` and `wsitrain` have no such split and ignore the
option.

If a tool you expect is absent from `<engine>_list_tools`, check whether it is
experimental before concluding the image is wrong.

---

## 7. Engines Are Independent

Each runs in its own container on its own port, so several can run at once —
for example `wsinsight` producing cell tables while `hplot` analyses an earlier
result. Stopping one does not affect the others.

The natural chains:

```
wsinsight   -> CSV / GeoJSON  ->  hplot        (boundary profiling)
sptxinsight -> CSV / h5ad     ->  hplot
kurtorank   -> annotated.h5ad ->  sptxinsight  (spatial analysis)
kurtorank   -> assignment CSV ->  wsitrain     (train a head)
wsitrain    -> models/<t>/main -> wsinsight    (deploy via zoo_model_dir)
```

Because they share `/workspace`, point the downstream engine's `data_dir` at
the same host directory and the handoff needs no copying.

---

## 8. Troubleshooting

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
| ------- | ----- | --- |
| "Cannot reach the … MCP server" | Container not running | `<engine>_status`, then `<engine>_start` |
| Tools missing right after `_start` | Server still booting | Call `<engine>_list_tools` again |
| `'data_dir' is required` / "does not exist" | Missing or wrong host path | Pass an existing **host** directory |
| A path argument is not found inside the container | Host path passed to `_call` | Rewrite it relative to `/workspace` |
| Outputs owned by root | The mounted directory was root-owned to begin with | `_start` passes your uid/gid; fix the ownership of `data_dir` |
| Port already in use | Another container or process holds it | Pass a different `port` to `_start`, or set `CLAWSIGHT_<ENGINE>_PORT` |
| Expected tool absent from the catalog | It is experimental, or the image predates it | Start with `experimental: true`; otherwise check the image tag |
| `gpu_ids` rejected | Engine is CPU-only | `hplot` and `kurtorank` take no GPUs |
| Jobs contend / OOM | Unbounded concurrency | Set `max_concurrent` to the GPU count |
| Wrong parameter name | Guessed instead of discovered | `<engine>_list_tools({"tool": "<name>"})` |

---

## 9. Agent Decision Guide

```text
Which engine?
├─ whole-slide images (.svs/.ndpi/.tif)        → wsinsight
├─ AnnData / Xenium spatial transcriptomics    → sptxinsight
├─ raw Xenium needing cell types first         → kurtorank, then sptxinsight
├─ an existing per-layer table to test/plot    → hplot
└─ training a new cell-classification head     → wsitrain

Then, always:
1. <engine>_status        — is it already up?
2. <engine>_start         — with data_dir = the host dir holding the data
3. <engine>_list_tools    — with tool= for the one you intend to call
4. <engine>_call          — paths relative to /workspace
5. poll job_status via _call if a job_id came back
6. <engine>_stop          — when finished
```

### Key constraints for agents

1. **Start before anything else.** No other tool works until the container is
   running.
2. **Never guess parameter names.** `<engine>_list_tools({"tool": "..."})`
   returns the authoritative schema; the catalog is live, not hard-coded.
3. **All paths inside `arguments` are `/workspace`-relative.**
4. **Poll to a terminal state, and read `job_logs` before any retry.**
5. **One job at a time per container** unless you raised `max_concurrent`
   deliberately.
6. **`hplot` and `kurtorank` take no `gpu_ids`.**
7. **Stop containers you started** once the work is done.

---

## 10. Configuration

Per-engine overrides, all optional, all read from the environment:

```
CLAWSIGHT_<ENGINE>_IMAGE       e.g. huangchtw/wsinsight:v1.2
CLAWSIGHT_<ENGINE>_PORT
CLAWSIGHT_<ENGINE>_CONTAINER
CLAWSIGHT_<ENGINE>_MCP_URL     point at an already-running server
CLAWSIGHT_<ENGINE>_TIMEOUT_MS  default 300000
```

`<ENGINE>` is the engine name upper-cased with `-` replaced by `_`, e.g.
`CLAWSIGHT_WSINSIGHT_PORT`.

Use `CLAWSIGHT_<ENGINE>_MCP_URL` when the user already runs a server outside
Docker — then skip `_start` entirely and go straight to `_list_tools`.
